      "\n",
      "Finally, the very architecture of modern LLMs is designed to capture aggregate human linguistic and behavioral patterns. Trained on terabytes of text produced by millions of individuals, these models internalize the statistical regularities of human language, reasoning, and even cultural norms. When deployed as a control group, an LLM can thus simulate the collective response of a broad, demographically diverse population, providing a realistic benchmark that reflects the heterogeneity of real‑world humans without the ethical and logistical complications of assembling such a cohort. By leveraging LLMs as control groups, researchers gain a reproducible, transparent, and ethically sound foundation for comparison, accelerating discovery while preserving the rigor that scientific inquiry demands.\n",
