      "**Bottom line of the rebuttal:** The opposition conflates *model* with *subject*. An LLM is precisely the kind of *controlled, manipulable, reproducible* reference that experimental science demands. Its limitations are *known, quantifiable, and can be mitigated*; its strengths—scalability, cost‑efficiency, standardisation, and the ability to simulate aggregate human language patterns—are *unmatched* by any human control group.\n",
